{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"How Environment Sourcing Works","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Tightlip"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvFileDirective","doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/GettingStarted"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/Obfuscation"],"anchor":"Explanation"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/environmentsourcing"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvironmentSourcing"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why your env vars resolve the same way whether you build from Xcode, the terminal, or CI."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Env-var secret setups have a recurring failure mode: the variable works in your shell but Xcode can’t see it, or it works locally but not in CI, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"~\/.zshenv"},{"type":"text","text":" exports it fine but "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"xcodebuild"},{"type":"text","text":" from a launcher doesn’t pick it up."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tightlip addresses this by sourcing your shell init file itself, in a controlled subshell, every build."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"The Algorithm","type":"heading","anchor":"The-Algorithm"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For each build, the plugin:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sources the env file in a clean zsh subshell.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" By default this is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"~\/.zshenv"},{"type":"text","text":", sourced with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zsh -f"},{"type":"text","text":" (no startup files, no profile chain). The subshell captures the resulting environment as a snapshot."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Merges that snapshot with ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProcessInfo.processInfo.environment","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — the build’s own environment, including Xcode Scheme env vars and CI job env vars."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Resolves per-key conflicts in favor of ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProcessInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" A CI runner that explicitly exports "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"APP_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","text":" overrides anything "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"~\/.zshenv"},{"type":"text","text":" might have said."}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The result: identical resolution regardless of how the build was launched. Xcode.app from Finder, Conductor, VS Code, "},{"code":"xcodebuild","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from Terminal — same env vars seen, same generated file."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Failure Modes","type":"heading","anchor":"Failure-Modes"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The subshell sourcing has a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"5-second timeout"}]},{"type":"text","text":". If sourcing fails (the file doesn’t exist, the file errors out, or it just takes too long), the tool falls back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProcessInfo"},{"type":"text","text":" alone and writes a single "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"note:"},{"type":"text","text":" to stderr identifying the file."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This means CI runners with no "},{"code":"~\/.zshenv","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" work unchanged — the fallback kicks in immediately and the job’s "},{"code":"env:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block is the sole source of values."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Slow `.zshenv` Cases","type":"heading","anchor":"Slow-zshenv-Cases"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tools like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mise"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"asdf"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"direnv"},{"type":"text","text":" invoked during "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".zshenv"},{"type":"text","text":" can push past the 5-second budget. If you see the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"note: sourcing \/path\/to\/file ... using process environment only"},{"type":"text","text":" message and weren’t expecting it, reproduce with:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["zsh -f -c 'source ~\/.zshenv'"],"syntax":"bash","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If that hangs or errors, your shell init is the cause. Move slow tools out of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".zshenv"},{"type":"text","text":" (into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".zshrc"},{"type":"text","text":", which the plugin doesn’t read), or point Tightlip at a smaller sidecar file with the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"envFile directive"}],"overridingTitle":"envFile directive","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvFileDirective"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/Obfuscation":{"abstract":[{"text":"What the XOR encoding actually protects against, and what it doesn’t.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/Obfuscation","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/obfuscation","title":"Obfuscation and Threat Model","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/EnvFileDirective":{"kind":"article","title":"Overriding the Sourced Env File","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/envfiledirective","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvFileDirective","abstract":[{"text":"Point Tightlip at a different shell-init file with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"envFile:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directive.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/GettingStarted":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the plugin to a target, drop in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Secrets.yml"},{"type":"text","text":", and start reading secrets at compile time."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/gettingstarted","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/GettingStarted","title":"Getting Started with Tightlip"},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore","abstract":[{"text":"A SwiftPM build-tool plugin that generates a typed Swift ","type":"text"},{"code":"Secrets","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" enum from environment variables at build time.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"Tightlip","kind":"symbol"}}}